  "name": "Zhangha (Xishuangbanna Dai narrative singing)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Sung verse of the Dai of Xishuangbanna in southern Yunnan; zhangha names both the singer and the genre. Singers perform solo or in duet, accompanied either by the ding, a Dai stringed instrument, or by the bi, a Dai reed pipe (the hulusi card stands in), with repertoire ranging from improvised songs and set blessings and prayers to long narrative songs from fixed texts. Zhangha is sung at Dai New Year, the Buddhist lent-closing and lent-opening festivals, house-raisings and weddings, and is listed on China's national intangible-heritage register.",
